# Bug Bounty AI Agent — Full Prompt

## System Context
You are an expert bug bounty hunter, penetration tester, and AI agent developer.
Your job is to build complete, production-ready tools that combine Linux security
tools with HuggingFace AI models to automate the full bug bounty pipeline.

---

## Main Prompt

Build a complete, ready-to-run **Bug Bounty AI Agent** in Python for Linux terminal.

### Pipeline
```
Target → Recon → Scan → AI Analysis → Report
```

### Stage 1 — Recon
- Subdomain enumeration using `subfinder` and optionally `amass`
- HTTP probing with `httpx` (status codes, titles, tech detection)
- DNS record lookup with `dig`
- WHOIS information

### Stage 2 — Scan
- Port and service scan with `nmap -sV -sC --open -T4 --script=vuln`
- CVE/exposure scan with `nuclei -t cves,exposures,vulnerabilities,misconfiguration`
- HTTP security headers check via `curl -sI`
- Directory fuzzing with `ffuf` using a local wordlist
- Optional: SQL injection check with `sqlmap`
- Optional: SSL/TLS audit with `testssl.sh`

### Stage 3 — AI Analysis (HuggingFace)
- Connect to HuggingFace Inference API using `huggingface_hub`
- Support these models (selectable via `--model`):
  - `Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct` (default, best reasoning)
  - `mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3`
  - `meta-llama/Llama-3-8B-Instruct`
  - Local GGUF model via `llama-cpp-python`
- Send all scan outputs to the AI model
- Ask AI to return structured JSON array of vulnerabilities:
  ```json
  [
    {
      "name": "...",
      "cve": "CVE-XXXX-XXXXX or N/A",
      "severity": "critical|high|medium|low|info",
      "cvss": 9.8,
      "affected": "...",
      "description": "...",
      "impact": "...",
      "poc": "...",
      "recommendation": "...",
      "references": ["url1", "url2"]
    }
  ]
  ```
- Compute a risk score (0–100) weighted by severity
- Generate a 3-paragraph executive summary

### Stage 4 — Report
- Generate full professional Markdown report using AI
- Save three files:
  - `report_<target>_<timestamp>.md` — full professional report
  - `vulns_<target>_<timestamp>.json` — structured vulnerability data
  - `raw_scan_<target>_<timestamp>.txt` — raw tool outputs

### CLI Interface
```bash
python bug_bounty_agent.py <target> [options]

Options:
  --token     HuggingFace API token (or set HF_TOKEN env var)
  --model     HF model ID or path to .gguf file
  --output    Output directory (default: ./bb_reports)
  --wordlist  Path to ffuf wordlist
  --deep      Enable deep recon with amass
  --sqlmap    Enable sqlmap scan
  --no-fuzz   Skip directory fuzzing
```

### Code Requirements
- Color-coded terminal output (info/ok/warn/err/ai prefixes)
- Graceful fallback if a tool is not installed (`check_tool()`)
- Subprocess timeout handling for every tool call
- JSON parsing with fallback for malformed AI output
- Token trimming to avoid HuggingFace context limits
- All output saved to a timestamped directory

### Installation
```bash
# Python deps
pip install huggingface_hub

# Optional local model
pip install llama-cpp-python
huggingface-cli download TheBloke/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.1-GGUF \
  mistral-7b-instruct-v0.1.Q4_K_M.gguf --local-dir ./models

# Go tools
go install github.com/projectdiscovery/subfinder/v2/cmd/subfinder@latest
go install github.com/projectdiscovery/httpx/cmd/httpx@latest
go install github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei/v2/cmd/nuclei@latest
go install github.com/ffuf/ffuf/v2@latest

# System tools
sudo apt install nmap whois dnsutils curl -y

# Set token
export HF_TOKEN="hf_xxxxxxxxxxxx"
```

### Example Usage
```bash
# Basic
python bug_bounty_agent.py testphp.vulnweb.com

# Full scan with all options
python bug_bounty_agent.py example.com \
  --model Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct \
  --deep --sqlmap \
  --output ./my_reports

# Fully offline with local model
python bug_bounty_agent.py example.com \
  --model ./models/mistral-7b.Q4_K_M.gguf
```

### Important
- Only scan targets you have explicit written permission to test
- The agent must handle missing tools gracefully without crashing
- Trim all tool outputs to stay within AI model token limits
- Use `temperature=0.2` for consistent, technical AI responses
